---
/** Plain-language explanation shown before a player opts in to tracking. */
---

<div class="grid gap-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-silver-300 sm:grid-cols-2">
  <div>
    <h4 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] text-silver-100 uppercase">What the host can see</h4>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
      <li>Your username and whether tracking is on.</li>
      <li>The results recorded for you: date, stakes, buy-in, rebuys and top-ups, cash-out and net result.</li>
      <li>
        Not your password. The website doesn’t show your email address to the host, though as the
        site’s operator the host can technically see account emails in the database admin tools. They
        are only used to send account emails.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h4 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] text-silver-100 uppercase">What the host can do</h4>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
      <li>Only the host can enter, correct or delete results. You can’t edit them yourself.</li>
      <li>Every change is permanently logged with the time and a reason.</li>
      <li>Other players can never see your results, and nothing is ever published.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="sm:col-span-2">
    <h4 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] text-silver-100 uppercase">If you change your mind</h4>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Turn tracking off at any time and your results disappear from your dashboard straight away, and the
      host can’t link new results to you. You can also remove your history from your account entirely.
      The amounts stay in the host’s table records, but without your name. Past sessions recorded before
      you opt in are never linked to you automatically.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
